## Final Judgement
**Summary:** The fact-check reveals that while Ambre Allinckx did not participate in the 2020 World Junior Squash Championships in Chennai, India, multiple credible sources—including clarifications from her parents and statements from tournament organizers—explicitly deny that safety concerns were the reason. Her parents stated they "never were concerned about safety in India" and attributed her absence to family scheduling and workload management, calling reports of safety reasons a "lie or journalistic invention."

**Conclusion:** The recorded evidence directly and clearly contradicts the claim that Ambre Allinckx refused to play in India due to safety reasons. Therefore, the claim is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
Based on the fact-check, the claim is refuted as Ambre Allinckx's parents explicitly denied that safety concerns in India were the reason for her withdrawal from the 2020 World Junior Squash Championships in Chennai. They clarified the absence was due to a pre-planned family holiday and workload management, terming safety reports a "lie or journalistic invention." This denial was corroborated by the [Squash Rackets Federation of India](https://indianexpress.com/article/sports/sport-others/there-wasnt-any-safety-concerns-in-india-swiss-squash-players-ambre-allinckx-parents-clarify-5270280/), and the [World Squash Federation](https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/more-sports/others/word-squash-federation-backs-india-on-security-at-junior-championship/articleshow/65069249.cms) stated that over 250 participants from 28 countries had "complete confidence" in the event's security.